    "body": "I've also changed a bit the code style because most of the file is using `TYPE *NAME` instead of `TYPE* NAME` declarations. And also, there were already inconsistencies in the affected functions. I've also changed `_XMLParser_CAST` into `XMLParserObject_CAST` because it's easier to remember `<NAME>_<CAST>` instead of `<SOMETHING_ELSE>_<CAST>` (anyway it was *me* who introduced that macro last year but I didn't think of that at that time).\r\n\r\nReview without whitespace changes: https://github.com/python/cpython/pull/132265/files?diff=split&w=1.\r\n\r\n<!-- gh-issue-number: gh-132097 -->\r\n* Issue: gh-132097\r\n<!-- /gh-issue-number -->\r\n",
